{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Elohim spoke all these words, saying.</b> It mentions both דִּבּוּר (speaking) and אֲמִירָה (saying) — one harsh and one soft. That is, as it is written: ״כֹּה תֹאמַר לְבֵית יַעֲקֹב״ (Exodus 19:3) — these are the women, say to them in a soft tone; ״וְתַגֵּיד לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — to the males, hard things like sinews. For this reason these are called עֲשֶׂרֶת הַדִּבְּרוֹת (the Ten Words/Sayings), while the entire creation of the world is called עֲשָׂרָה מַאֲמָרוֹת (ten utterances), because all the works of Creation were created בְּצִבְיוֹנָם — that is, in those forms that they chose for themselves — which is אֲמִירָה רַכָּה, a soft saying without decree. But the commandments of HaShem are all a decree of the King, for a person does not say 'it is impossible for me to eat pork and my soul loathes it,' but rather 'it is possible, and the Holy One, blessed be He, has decreed it upon me' — this is דִּבּוּר קָשֶׁה, harsh speech. But in any case, for women, whose understanding is weaker, one must explain in a soft tone to make known to them the benefit of the commandments, for every person of understanding accepts upon himself the decrees of the Holy One, blessed be He, while the weak of understanding need explanation, so that they may be בְּצִבְיוֹנָם. And even in the creation of heaven and earth it is written (Psalms 33:6): ״בִּדְבַר ה׳ שָׁמַיִם נַעֲשׂוּ״ etc. — because they possess understanding, therefore they would accept upon themselves the decree of HaShem, blessed be He, even not בְּצִבְיוֹנָם. But concerning the lower beings it says (Psalms 33:8–9): ״יִירְאוּ מֵה׳ כָּל הָאָרֶץ, כִּי הוּא אָמַר וַיֶּהִי״ — which means: He said to them a soft saying, and they were created בְּצִבְיוֹנָם. But concerning the upper beings we find a rebuke, as it says (Genesis 1:6): ״יְהִי רָקִיעַ״, for ״תֵּחַת גְּעָרָה בְּמֵבִין״ (Proverbs 17:10). And likewise Moses said (Deuteronomy 32:1): ״הַאֲזִינוּ הַשָּׁמַיִם וַאֲדַבֵּרָה, וְתִשְׁמַע הָאָרֶץ אִמְרֵי פִי״. And the language of דִּבּוּר and אֲמִירָה fits well, whether He is speaking simply of heaven and earth, or whether He is speaking toward people who are high and exalted like the height of the heavens, and toward the peoples of the earth." "And these words were ten, to teach that upon them the world stands, since it was created with ten utterances, so as to reveal the existences of ten sefirot without whatness, and further so as to exact punishment from the wicked etc. For they say to the wicked: you should have taken to heart that the world was not created in vain with ten utterances, but rather because its endurance depends on the עֲשֶׂרֶת הַדִּבְּרוֹת that encompass the entire Torah, as Rashi explained at the end of parashat Mishpatim (Exodus 24:12) — and if so, by transgressing them you destroy a full world, and for this reason it is fitting to exact punishment from them etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:34.846874600Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}